 "text": " What if you jumped into a hole straight through the Earth? The deepest hole we've ever dug is in Russia. 12 kilometers. It took 20 years, and the rock at the bottom reached 180 degrees. Your hole goes all the way through. 12,700 kilometers. You jump. Gravity pulls you faster and faster. By the centre, you're doing 8 kilometers a second. That's London to Moscow in five minutes. Around you, the core is about 6,000 degrees, as hot as the surface of the sun. Now gravity flips. It pulls you back, slowing you down, until you float up out of the other side and stop, right at the surface. Total trip, 38 minutes. Miss the edge and you fall back in, back and forth, forever, like a pendulum. Unless there's air in the tunnel, then drag steals a little speed on every trip and you end up stuck, floating at the very centre of the Earth. Subscribe for more What Ifs.",
